::Question 1::
What type of error is raised when you try to divide a number by zero in Python? 
{ 
~ IndexError
~ ValueError 
= ZeroDivisionError 
~ TypeError
}

::Question 2::
Which of the following errors occurs when you try to access an index that is out of range for a sequence (e.g., a list or a string)? 
{ 
~ KeyError
= IndexError
~ SyntaxError
~ AttributeError
}

::Question 3::
If you try to access a dictionary key that does not exist, which error will be raised? 
{ 
~ ValueError
~ TypeError
~ AttributeError
= KeyError
}

::Question 4::
What type of error is raised when the Python interpreter encounters code that does not conform to the language's syntax rules? 
{ 
= SyntaxError
~ NameError
~ IndentationError 
~ TypeError
}

::Question 5::
Which of the following errors is raised when you try to perform an operation on an object that is not supported or appropriate for its data type? 
{ 
~ ValueError
~ AttributeError
~ IndexError
= TypeError
}
